
## A second forest, and a laser that met leaves

Nothing above separates a failed calibration from a failed method, because one
site cannot. The second pairing is Quebec's permanent sample plot network under
the province's open lidar, where the plots are 400 square metre circles, the
canopy height models are published by map sheet, and every acquisition carries
the year it was flown. Plots were kept only where the field measurement and the
flight fall within two years of each other.

```{r qc-load}
qc <- read.csv("../data/qc_lidar_plots.csv")

qc_n <- nrow(qc)
qc_sheets <- length(unique(qc$feuillet))
qc_gap <- mean(qc$gap)
qc_r <- cor(qc$ba_ha, qc$h_p95)
qc_ba <- mean(qc$ba_ha)
```

The sample held `r qc_n` plots across `r qc_sheets` map sheets, with a mean gap
of `r round(qc_gap, 1)` years between the field visit and the flight, a mean
basal area of `r round(qc_ba, 1)` square metres per hectare, and a correlation
between basal area and the 95th height percentile of `r round(qc_r, 2)`.

```{r qc-cv}
qc_form <- as.formula(paste("ba_ha ~", paste(predictors, collapse = " + ")))

set.seed(2026)
qc_folds <- sample(rep(1:10, length.out = nrow(qc)))
qc_pred <- numeric(nrow(qc))
for (k in 1:10) {
  qc_pred[qc_folds == k] <- predict(
    ranger(qc_form, qc[qc_folds != k, ], num.trees = 500, seed = 2026),
    qc[qc_folds == k, ])$predictions
}
qc_rmse_random <- rmse(qc$ba_ha, qc_pred)
qc_r2 <- 1 - qc_rmse_random^2 / var(qc$ba_ha)

qc_sf <- st_as_sf(qc, coords = c("x", "y"), crs = 32198, remove = FALSE)
qc_knndm <- knndm(qc_sf, k = 10, clustering = "kmeans")

qc_pred_sp <- numeric(nrow(qc))
for (k in seq_along(qc_knndm$indx_test)) {
  test_rows <- qc_knndm$indx_test[[k]]
  train_rows <- qc_knndm$indx_train[[k]]
  qc_pred_sp[test_rows] <- predict(
    ranger(qc_form, qc[train_rows, ], num.trees = 500, seed = 2026),
    qc[test_rows, ])$predictions
}
qc_rmse_spatial <- rmse(qc$ba_ha, qc_pred_sp)

qc_unc_rmse <- 100 * qc_rmse_spatial / qc_ba
qc_ci <- 100 * (qc_rmse_spatial / sqrt(qc_n)) * 1.645 / qc_ba
```

Random folds returned a root mean square error of
`r round(qc_rmse_random, 2)` square metres per hectare, an explained variance of
`r round(qc_r2, 3)`. Folds chosen by nearest neighbour distance matching, which
spaces the held-out plots so that the distances they face resemble the distances
a real prediction faces, returned `r round(qc_rmse_spatial, 2)`, a difference of
`r round(100 * (qc_rmse_spatial - qc_rmse_random) / qc_rmse_random, 1)` per cent.
